From b42ffccd90447bf7c08ea0139af334aeff705d75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Het <hetzel30@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:48:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] test+build: current API, stale-golden guard, shared-pool
 equivalence; macOS build script

- ProdMiner now instantiates from the score_bpp9000.h production
  constants (the 9-arg pre-trimode instantiation no longer compiles).
- runGolden uses Rating::error and one shared random2 pool per seed
  group (setPool) instead of a ~512MB pool per worker thread.
- The committed CSV goldens predate the trimode merge: row 0 of
  gt_production.csv scores 4811 with the current code on BOTH x86_64
  and ARM64 (bit-identical) vs 4254 in the file, and the ant nonces
  carry no mode bits. Guarded behind QINER_ENABLE_STALE_CSV_GOLDENS
  (expected to fail on every platform until regenerated with
  tools/bpp9000_ground_truth.cpp). The deriveRootANN digest vectors
  are current and stay active.
- Chain replay updated to the current API (parentANN+parentShift,
  getBestANN, root from the identity pubkey) under the same guard.
- New test: shared pool vs owned pool must yield identical Ratings -
  pins the pool-sharing change in Qiner.
- build-macos.sh: arm64/x86_64/universal builds with plain clang++.
